{"causes": ["The unification of Upper and Lower Egypt around 3100 BCE led to the establishment of a centralized religious system that revered Horus as a national symbol.", "The construction of monumental architecture, such as the pyramids, necessitated protective symbols like the Eye of Horus for the afterlife of pharaohs.", "The socio-political structure of ancient Egypt, emphasizing divine kingship, elevated Horus and his symbol to represent royal authority and protection."], "effects": ["The Eye of Horus became a ubiquitous symbol in ancient Egyptian artifacts, influencing their art, religion, and burial practices throughout the Dynastic periods.", "It contributed to the development of a complex system of Egyptian mathematics, where its fractions were used in practical applications like measuring land and grain.", "The symbol's enduring legacy has inspired countless interpretations and adaptations in modern art and culture, reflecting its timeless significance. "], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "horus", "sourceName": "Horus", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "eye-of-horus", "targetName": "Eye of Horus", "context": "The deity Horus is credited with the creation of the Eye of Horus as a protective symbol following his battle against Set."}, {"sourceSlug": "ancient-egypt", "sourceName": "Ancient Egypt", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "eye-of-horus", "targetName": "Eye of Horus", "context": "The Eye of Horus is a fundamental element within the religious practices of ancient Egypt, particularly in funerary contexts."}, {"sourceSlug": "ancient-egypt", "sourceName": "Ancient Egypt", "verb": "DEFINES", "targetSlug": "protection-in-ancient-egypt", "targetName": "Protection in Ancient Egypt", "context": "The Eye of Horus defines the concept of protection in ancient Egyptian belief systems, symbolizing health and safety."}, {"sourceSlug": "pyramid-texts", "sourceName": "Pyramid Texts", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "eye-of-horus", "targetName": "Eye of Horus", "